    intro: "A spreadsheet saves time only when it helps you reject weak options early. Opening twenty Hacoo links without a method usually produces twenty different titles, image sets and size charts that are difficult to compare. A better workflow is smaller: define the product, choose the evidence that matters, keep a two- or three-item shortlist and use the current page as the final reference. The process below is designed for ordinary shoppers, not data analysts. It uses a simple decision record that can be kept in a note on your phone.",
