        "Tracking wording can be confusing. ‘Label created’ may not mean the carrier has the parcel. ‘In transit’ can cover several international stages. ‘Out for delivery’ relates to the local delivery attempt, while ‘delivered’ should be checked against the drop-off location and household. Read the carrier’s own definition when available instead of assuming every status has the same meaning.",
